2026-09-27T04:47:39.0955545Z Description:
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0956021Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0956460Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0957957Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0959317Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0959446Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0959737Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0960138Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0960587Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0960712Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0961010Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0961202Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0961419Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0961951Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0962284Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0962443Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0962860Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0963107Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0963301Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0963866Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0964370Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0965346Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0966242Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0966417Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0967298Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0968179Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0968691Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0969194Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0969877Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0970295Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0970656Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0970895Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0973363Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0975856Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0976215Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0977331Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0978291Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0979383Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0980410Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0981247Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0981792Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0982572Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0982992Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0983235Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0985183Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0989570Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0991080Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:39.0992654Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:39.1063812Z 
